WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.250
We missed a collection in February.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.720
I don't think people realise
what that does to a family.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.200
How many had you missed?

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.280
One.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.020
You want to catch these things early.

6
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:22.220
Like any great business, we focus on doing
one thing exceptionally well.

7
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.050
The bins?

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.560
We don't even do recycling yet.

9
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:34.630
I'd never written code. With Code Overlord,
I had lorry detection working by lunchtime.

10
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.140
One minion tracks the vehicle. Another sends the alert.

11
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.740
The grunts write the code.

12
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.710
We now have eleven cameras,

13
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.300
thermal imaging and a dedicated server in the garage.

14
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.250
For one bin?

15
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.760
At this stage.

16
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.180
It worked beautifully.

17
00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.780
Four collections.

18
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.880
Then I added two-way audio.

19
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.700
Just six inches to the left, please.
You're outside the collection zone.

20
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:09.840
You what?

21
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.720
That's when Dave became aware of the platform.

22
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.920
[BLEEP]

23
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.940
[BLEEP] off, camera [BLEEP]!

24
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.240
[CONTINUOUS BLEEP]

25
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.380
They tried written abuse.

26
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.440
Bin [BLEEP].

27
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.890
It read that correctly.

28
00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:34.760
So I asked Code Overlord for an incident-monitoring minion.

29
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:39.130
It now sends me everything that needs reviewing.

30
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.270
How much is there?

31
00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.560
Quite a lot of Dave.

32
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.640
What's this cost you?

33
00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.740
Fourteen thousand pounds.

34
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.980
Review this!

35
00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.930
The software's been excellent.

36
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.030
The binmen are another matter.

37
00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.300
I'm suing the [BLEEP].
